html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/commit/068cfeb8404ce797f2c7268d82c286da60caf737"},{"sha":"813a3f9b98ac90c24457b25eb2aeb3c12eae8eef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/commits/813a3f9b98ac90c24457b25eb2aeb3c12eae8eef","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/commit/813a3f9b98ac90c24457b25eb2aeb3c12eae8eef"}]},{"sha":"ba11002958ec25236599a8f8bfb31afad429a57c","node_id":"C_kwDOSbOoU9oAKGJhMTEwMDI5NThlYzI1MjM2NTk5YThmOGJmYjMxYWZhZDQyOWE1N2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"konard","email":"drakonard@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-05T04:01:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"konard","email":"drakonard@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-05T04:01:50Z"},"message":"Merge origin/main into the #905 branch\n\nThe #905 fixes that landed on main (the shell-envelope exit-code reader,\n`failed_verification`, and the `strip_clause_lead` content parser) supersede\nthis branch's earlier versions of the same three defects, so main's\nimplementation is kept for all of them.\n\nWhat this branch still adds on top is the part main does not cover: the\n`is_error` metadata a client attaches to a tool result survives the\nOpenAI-compatible, Anthropic and Responses surfaces; `Progress` separates an\nobserved attempt from a satisfied step; and the general-change execution state\nmachine recovers a rejected write with one read plus one bounded retry before\nreporting the observed failure.\n\n`plan_general_change_step` keeps its move into `general_execution`, with main's\nverification gate ported into both its failure branch and its completion path.\n`plain_nonzero_status` is dropped: main's shell-envelope parser reads the same\nexit codes structurally. Generated artifacts (self-AST census, planner\nfixtures, total-closure shards) are regenerated from the merged sources.","tree":{"sha":"45006ae9f0069629bea8bc6d472f73fbfeaac5ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/git/trees/45006ae9f0069629bea8bc6d472f73fbfeaac5ee"},"url":"https://api